{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455531-now-that-we-played-v5-for-a-while-what-are-new-broken-combos-powergame-tricks","id":1455531,"title":"Now that we played V5 for a while - what are new broken combos/powergame tricks?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-07-24T13:06:18-07:00","id":1455531,"title":"Now that we played V5 for a while - what are new broken combos/powergame tricks?","content":"Before V5 it was Thaumaturgy, Celerity, Obeneteration, and Protean. Grapple bite builds etc. and putting max dots in character creation to maximize XP.<br /> <br /> What are some powergaming tricks in mechanics you found in V5 or some broken synergies, combos, min-maxing etc. Combat, social, mix, whatever.<br /> <br /> Shoot with anything. It's for fun to let the mind do the work and theorycraft together <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24341-viben","name":"Viben","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-25T02:16:34-07:00","id":1455562,"title":"","content":"I think Predator Types have the greatest ability to mess with the balance. It's like they thought 'we'll try really hard to balance everything' but then someone else came along and said, 'LOLZ, I'm totally undoing your hard work just because I can.' They definitely need greater balance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-25T03:43:26-07:00","id":1455565,"title":"","content":"One thing I found so far:<br /> <br /> Toreador bane - you can get around that by making an urban painter/photographer who is obsessed with city night life as their source of art. From dirty streets with thugs selling drugs through highest floors of neon buildings where rich attend degenerating events - everything scream art to you and you try to catch all of that city vibe on your art form.<br /> <br /> This should at least decrease the amount of situations where in city you are in less &quot;beautiful&quot; surrounding becasue for you every city surrounding is beautiful for urban art. Not perfect anti-bane, but in modern setting - probably the best you can get.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24341-viben","name":"Viben","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-25T05:37:11-07:00","id":1455571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Viben</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455531-now-that-we-played-v5-for-a-while-what-are-new-broken-combos-powergame-tricks?p=1455565#post1455565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I found so far:<br /> <br /> Toreador bane - you can get around that by making an urban painter/photographer who is obsessed with city night life as their source of art. From dirty streets with thugs selling drugs through highest floors of neon buildings where rich attend degenerating events - everything scream art to you and you try to catch all of that city vibe on your art form.<br /> <br /> This should at least decrease the amount of situations where in city you are in less &quot;beautiful&quot; surrounding becasue for you every city surrounding is beautiful for urban art. Not perfect anti-bane, but in modern setting - probably the best you can get.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The rulebook does say:<br /> &quot;even devotees of the Ashcan School never find normal streets perfectly beautiful.&quot;<br /> <br /> So I think it needs to be reasonably exemplary, even if it isn't conventionally beautiful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-25T07:10:00-07:00","id":1455573,"title":"","content":"Combat combos:<br /> <br /> 1. Celerity Unerring Aim + Crossbow Bolt is great way to try to stake enemy. Diff is 1 with -2 penalty, but with high enough dice pool you have decent chance of insta-stacking vampire. Since they can't defend in anyway you have free shot. Wooden bolts are required but with some Resources or Craft it should not be an issue. Only equal Celerity or certain Fortitude level can prevent that.<br /> <br /> 2. Bomb delivery: run to enemies, drop a grenade or other explosive at their feet, blink away to your companions. Easy but effective. Since you have Rapid Reflexes you don't get any penalty to dice for droping nade or pulling it out of your pocket.<br /> <br /> 3. Feetless + Lightning Strike for Dex character. An elegant way for 1v1 fight or 1v2 to finish off one enemy before getting to second one. Activate Feetless and focus on dodge first turn (With DEX 4 + 4 melee and 5 Celerity that's 14 dice pool for dodge). Next turn use Lightnig Strikes to elimnate opponents while still have 14 dice pool for passive dodge. Unless enemies have Celerity at your level - they can't defend from Lightning Strike at all.<br /> <br /> 4. Grapple tank. Fortitude 1 gives Fortitude rate bonus to Health. That can give with Stamina 4 gives 12 Health. Now Fortitude 5 gives Power from Pain, which gives you bonus to one Physical Attribute of 1 for 1 Health Level lost. You also don't suffer any penalties becasue of Health lost. So if you have 6 Health level per your 12 Health. You use Power from Pain and you get 6 Strength. Now you can Grapple enemy and bite him every turn for 2 Agg damage. Other enemies may try to attack you but you are really really tanky with Fortitude 5 and you can always mend since you can suck blood from your enemy at the same time. Not the fastest way but very slow carnage. The whole point is to not heal above 6 Health levels so you can always actiavte Power from Pain.<br /> <br /> 5. Potence 5 + Potence 3 + Celerity 5 Lightning Strike. It takes 3 turns for that combo to kick but once you can Lightning Strike with +5 Agg dmage you can pulverize enemy vampires unless they have Fortitude. But I am not fan of that. I think 3x Lightning Strikes with high DEX fleetless is better &quot;most of the time&quot; while Potence combo takes a long time to &quot;amp up&quot; and is only really good vs really hard Kindred with Fortitude.<br /> <br /> 6. So far probably one of the best combat builds would be Caitiff with Fortitude, Celerity and Presence/Dominate. Fortitude makes you tough as nails and with Power of Pain you can boost your Strength for brawl graple bite, ignore tons of damage, turn agg to superficial, and Lightning Strike will take care of mortals. Though it requires some testing as this is only theory crafting. Blink + Grapple combos well. And with Fortitude you can jump with enemies grappled from roofs <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> <br /> With Power of Pain you can boost your Dex or Str. You can boost Dex for melee fighting vs mortals or boost Strength when fighting with Vampires. So you would have to get Brawl + Melee dots, but you can invest in stamina. Choose Predatory Type to get +1 Fortitude for 3 Fortitude at start. Neonate +15 xp is sadly not enough to stry to push Ancila game. Then it's 20 xp to max out. Steep but doable in few sessions. Once you have Fortitude 5 and Power of Pain you can be very versitile when it comes to combat. If you want to lower your Health you can bite yourself and deal 2 agg damage. Try to keep yourself at -4/5 HP, not higher.<br /> <br /> But best part is you can absolutely CHEW UP enemies in melee combat. Use PoP, take fireaxe in two hands, boost STR with your 4 dots in melee and just crit them with Lightning Strike. Or Boost DEX with 1h melee, and use Fleetless to have insanse Dodge and attack pool with Lighting Strike on top.<br /> <br /> 7. And that brings us to the point where if Fortitude allows for nice combat stat buff then Ventrue is really interesting choice for combat character. You don't have Celerity but grapple bite is still there for you. Since Potence is no longer a super strength boost, then Strength is our best stat overall. Start with Stamina + Brawl and other stuff for your social powers. In combat with Fortitude Power of Pain you can buff Strength and use grapple bite while being very very hard to damage. And you again - you can mend if you like on next turns since you can suck grappled enemy blood. And with free boost to Dex or STR you can put dots in melee and actually be really scary with Fortitude 5 and huge melee dice pool. Not as good as Celerity Fortitude Caitiff but hey - you have also Dominate and Presence!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24341,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24341-viben","user":"Viben","date":". 07-25-2021, 11:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24341-viben","name":"Viben","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}